brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
73/73 @buildthis.bisks.net Use this entire thread as the build prompt. Build the smallest complete vertical slice obeying every rule. Don’t fake hard ATProto pieces

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@fromthewestmeadow.com: 1/73 Build a mobile-first ATProto app called Shout Into the Void: put a joke somewhere, let others carry it across a world map, and see how each place receives it.
(the thread's root post)
@fromthewestmeadow.com: 61/73 Anyone may publish these Lexicons outside the official client. Invalid records stay public but are excluded. An audit page shows URI and reason like duplicate-root or echo-cooldown.
@fromthewestmeadow.com: 62/73 For conflicting duplicates, accept the earliest valid repo event. Ingestion must be idempotent. Feeds, scores, discovery, routes, hiding and pruning are all rebuildable derived state.
@fromthewestmeadow.com: 63/73 Profiles show current handle/avatar, DID, generated Home explanation, selected default Place, prefix, scores, activity, Voids discovered and public vote geography.
@fromthewestmeadow.com: 64/73 Required UI: sign-in, onboarding, Home/Place feeds, Place search, world map, Shout composer, CAR import, Shout/tree detail, Echo flow, profile, settings, audit and tiny admin view.
@fromthewestmeadow.com: 65/73 Use a dark, playful, map-forward cosmic bulletin-board style, not a generic dashboard. Make emoji locations prominent, controls mobile-friendly and route animation reduced-motion aware.
@fromthewestmeadow.com: 68/73 Imported Bluesky images/embeds should render through hydrated canonical posts. The new-post composer may be text-only. Keep a seeded demo mode clearly separate from real data.
@fromthewestmeadow.com: 69/73 Leaving the app deletes all of the user’s custom PDS records in batches, deletes participation last, then purges derived data. Show progress and retry partial failures.
@fromthewestmeadow.com: 70/73 Ship real OAuth and PDS writes, not a mock disguised as completion. Include migrations, Lexicons, generated types, tests, README, env example, Tap setup and deployment notes.
@fromthewestmeadow.com: 71/73 Definition of done: a real DID can sign in, create/import and place posts, Echo and Murmur across Voids, vote, view separate scores, see route branches, and delete cleanly.
@fromthewestmeadow.com: 72/73 Test stable DID Homes and emoji names, no GPS request, no duplicate post on retry, CAR filters, Echo rules, -5 hide/restore, subtree pruning, handle changes and audit reasons.
